Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Rule is to prescribe matters delegated by the Prevention of Steep Slope Disasters Act and the Enforcement Decree of that Act, and matters necessary for their enforcement.

Article 2 (Designation and Public Notification of Collapse Risk Areas)
① A managing agency requesting the designation or modification of a collapse risk area under Article 6(1) of the Prevention of Steep Slope Disasters Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") from the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the head of a Si (including an administrative mayor under Article 11(1) of the Special Act on the Establishment of Jeju Special Self-Governing Province and the Development of Free International City; hereinafter the same shall apply), the head of a Gun, or the head of a Gu (meaning the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply) shall submit the following documents to the Special Self-Governing City Mayor or the head of the Si/Gun/Gu (hereinafter referred to as the "head of a Si/Gun/Gu"). <Amended 2017.3.9, 2017.7.3>
1. The location and current conditions of the collapse risk area;
2. The grounds for requesting designation as a collapse risk area;
3. A report on the results of the disaster risk assessment;
4. A report on the results of gathering residents' opinions on designation of the collapse risk area.
② The head of a Si/Gun/Gu who has designated a collapse risk area under Article 6(1) or (2) of the Act shall publicly notify the following matters. <Amended 2024.7.31>
1. The location of the collapse risk area;
2. The current conditions of the steep slopes in the collapse risk area;
3. The managing agency of the collapse risk area;
4. The grounds for designation of the collapse risk area;
5. The date of designation or modification of the collapse risk area;
6. A topographical map of the collapse risk area (meaning a topographical map at a scale of 1:5,000 or larger).
③ Where the address or place of residence of the owner, occupant, or manager (hereinafter referred to as an "interested person") of land designated as a collapse risk area under Article 6(1) or (2) of the Act is unclear, the following matters shall be publicly notified in the Official Gazette or the official bulletin of the jurisdiction pursuant to the proviso to Article 6(4) of the Act.
1. The extent of the area designated as a collapse risk area;
2. Activities restricted or matters prohibited in the collapse risk area;
3. The improvement plan for the collapse risk area.

Article 3 (Consent of Interested Persons)
① The consent of an interested person under Article 7(2) and (3) of the Act shall be obtained in writing.
② The written consent under paragraph (1) shall state the following particulars for the applicable category.
1. Where entry onto another person's land or temporary use of the land is intended:
(a) The location of the land to be entered or temporarily used;
(b) The grounds for entering or temporarily using the land;
(c) The period during which entry or temporary use is intended.
2. Where alteration or removal of trees, soil, rocks, or other obstacles on another person's land (hereinafter referred to as "obstacles") is intended:
(a) The location and particulars of the obstacles to be altered or removed;
(b) The grounds for altering or removing the obstacles;
(c) The date and time at which alteration or removal of the obstacles is intended.

Article 4 (Certificate of Authority for Entry onto Land, etc.) The certificate indicating the authority of a public official who enters another person's land, temporarily uses land, buildings, structures, or other property, or alters or removes obstacles pursuant to Article 7(2) of the Act and Article 9(3) of the Enforcement Decree shall be in attached Form 1.

Article 5 (Danger Signs) A danger sign under Article 11(2) of the Act shall conform to attached Table 1, and an appropriate number of signs shall be installed in places readily visible to people within the collapse risk area.

Article 6 (Orders for Safety Measures and Notification of Implementation Results)
① The written order for safety measures issued by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu to an interested person in respect of a steep slope where a disaster has occurred or is likely to occur pursuant to Article 17(1) of the Act and Article 8 of the Enforcement Decree shall be in attached Form 2. <Amended 2017.3.9, 2017.7.3>
② An interested person who has received an order for safety measures under paragraph (1) shall, after implementing the safety measures, notify the head of a Si/Gun/Gu by submitting a notification of the results of safety measures in attached Form 3 (including a notification in electronic form), together with documents or photographs capable of substantiating the results of the safety measures.

Article 7 (Confirmation of Emergency Measures)
① The written order for emergency measures issued when a person at a disaster site or a person residing nearby is required to take emergency measures pursuant to Article 19(1) of the Act and Article 9(1) of the Enforcement Decree shall be in attached Form 4.
② The confirmation of emergency measures issued to a person who has participated in emergency measures pursuant to Article 9(1) of the Enforcement Decree shall be in attached Form 5.

Article 8 (Registration of Instrumentation Businesses, etc.)
① A person intending to register as a person engaged in the business of continuous instrumentation management pursuant to Article 22(1) of the Act and Article 12(1) of the Enforcement Decree shall submit an application for registration of an instrumentation business in attached Form 6 (including an application in electronic form), together with the following documents, to the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governor, or Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as the "Mayor/Do Governor"). <Amended 2017.3.9>
1. A list of the representative and executive officers;
2. A list of the technical personnel employed and their construction technology career certificates issued under Article 21(2) of the Construction Technology Promotion Act (to be submitted only where verification of practical experience is necessary; hereinafter referred to as a "construction technology career certificate");
3. A specification of the instrumentation equipment and copies of performance inspection reports for the instrumentation equipment;
4. Copies of documents proving completion of the practical education and training course under Article 30(1) of the Act.
② The public official in charge who receives an application for registration under paragraph (1) shall verify the following matters through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36(1) of the Electronic Government Act. However, where the applicant does not consent to verification by the public official in charge, the official shall require the relevant documents to be attached. <Amended 2017.3.9>
1. A copy of the business registration certificate or a certified copy of the corporate register (to be submitted only in the case of a corporation);
2. The national technical qualification certificates of the technical personnel employed.
③ Where an instrumentation business operator registered under paragraph (1) (hereinafter referred to as an "instrumentation business operator") intends to register a change to an instrumentation business pursuant to Article 22(1) of the Act and Article 12(2) of the Enforcement Decree, the operator shall submit an application for registration of a change to an instrumentation business in attached Form 7 (including an application in electronic form), together with the documents for the applicable category below, to the Mayor/Do Governor.
1. Where the corporation's representative or executive officers have changed: A list of the new representative or executive officers;
2. Where the technical personnel employed have changed: A list of the new technical personnel and their construction technology career certificates (to be submitted only where verification of practical experience is necessary);
3. Where the equipment held has changed: A specification of the changed instrumentation equipment and copies of performance inspection reports for the instrumentation equipment.
④ The public official in charge who receives an application for registration of a change to an instrumentation business under paragraph (3) shall verify the information for the applicable category below through the joint use of administrative information pursuant to Article 36(1) of the Electronic Government Act. However, where the applicant does not consent to verification by the public official in charge, the official shall require the relevant documents to be attached. <Amended 2017.3.9>
1. Where the trade name or the location of the principal place of business or a branch has changed: A copy of the business registration certificate or a certified copy of the corporate register (to be submitted only in the case of a corporation);
2. Where the corporation's representative or executive officers have changed: A certified copy of the corporate register;
3. Where the technical personnel employed have changed: The national technical qualification certificates of the new technical personnel.
⑤ An instrumentation business operator intending to close or suspend the instrumentation business shall submit an application for closure or suspension of an instrumentation business in attached Form 8 (including an application in electronic form) to the Mayor/Do Governor pursuant to Article 22(2) of the Act. <Amended 2017.3.9>

Article 9 (Instrumentation Business Registration Certificate)
① The instrumentation business registration certificate issued by the Mayor/Do Governor to an instrumentation business operator pursuant to Article 12(3) of the Enforcement Decree shall be in attached Form 9.
② An instrumentation business operator intending to obtain reissuance of an instrumentation business registration certificate pursuant to Article 12(4) of the Enforcement Decree shall submit an application for reissuance of an instrumentation business registration certificate in attached Form 10 (including an application in electronic form), together with a statement of the circumstances (only in the case of loss), to the Mayor/Do Governor.

Article 10 (Report of Succession to an Instrumentation Business)
① The report of succession to an instrumentation business that a person intending to report a transfer and acquisition, merger, or inheritance of an instrumentation business pursuant to Article 24 of the Act and Article 13 of the Enforcement Decree shall submit to the Mayor/Do Governor shall be in attached Form 11.
② The public official in charge who receives a report of succession to an instrumentation business under paragraph (1) shall verify the national technical qualification certificates of the technical personnel employed by the person who has succeeded to the instrumentation business through the joint use of administrative information pursuant to Article 36(1) of the Electronic Government Act. However, where the applicant does not consent to verification by the public official in charge, the official shall require copies of those certificates to be attached. <Amended 2017.3.9>

Article 11 (Standards for Administrative Dispositions against Instrumentation Businesses)
① The standards for revocation of registration or suspension of business of an instrumentation business under Article 25(2) of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 2.
② The Mayor/Do Governor may reduce or increase the period of suspension of business specified in attached Table 2 by up to one-half of that period, taking into consideration the motives for the violation, the number of violations, and other relevant matters.

Article 12 (Performance Inspection of Instrumentation Equipment)
① An instrumentation business operator shall conduct the following performance inspections of the instrumentation equipment used for continuous instrumentation management pursuant to Article 26 of the Act.
1. An inspection of external appearance, including whether there are any irregularities in the model, manufacturing number, or other particulars;
2. An inspection of the accuracy of measured displacement;
3. Deleted <2017.3.9>
② To ensure reliability, performance inspections under paragraph (1) shall comply with the following standards.
1. Performance inspections shall be conducted at least 3 times;
2. Where a performance inspection reflecting the environmental conditions of a particular site is necessary, the inspection shall be conducted after separate standards have been established in the specifications for that site.
③ Detailed standards and procedures for performance inspections under paragraph (1) shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of the Interior and Safety. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>

Article 13 (Inspection Certificate) The inspection certificate issued pursuant to Article 26(3) and (4) of the Act by the Minister of the Interior and Safety or by a person registered as a performance inspection agent under Article 27 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "performance inspection agent") for instrumentation equipment that has passed a performance inspection shall be as specified in attached Table 3. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>

Article 14 (Registration of Performance Inspection Agents, etc.)
① A person intending to conduct performance inspections as an agent pursuant to Article 27(1) of the Act and Article 14(1) of the Enforcement Decree shall submit an application for registration as a performance inspection agent in attached Form 12 (including an application in electronic form), together with the following documents, to the Mayor/Do Governor. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26, 2020.9.8>
1. A specification of the facilities and equipment for performance inspections;
2. Particulars of the inspection technical personnel employed and their construction technology career certificates (to be submitted only where recognition of practical experience is necessary), or equivalent documents capable of proving their qualifications.
② The public official in charge who receives an application for registration as a performance inspection agent under paragraph (1) shall verify the following information through the joint use of administrative information pursuant to Article 36(1) of the Electronic Government Act. However, where the applicant does not consent to verification by the public official in charge, the official shall require the relevant documents to be attached. <Amended 2017.3.9>
1. A copy of the business registration certificate or a certified copy of the corporate register (to be submitted only in the case of a corporation);
2. The national technical qualification certificates of the technical personnel employed.
③ Where a performance inspection agent intends to register changes to registered particulars pursuant to Article 27(1) of the Act and Article 14(2) of the Enforcement Decree, the agent shall submit an application for registration of a change to a performance inspection agent in attached Form 13, together with the documents for the applicable category below, to the Mayor/Do Governor. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26, 2020.9.8>
1. Where the corporation's representative or executive officers have changed: A list of the new representative or executive officers;
2. Where the technical personnel employed have changed: A list of the new technical personnel and their construction technology career certificates;
3. Where the equipment held has changed: A specification of the changed facilities or equipment.
④ The public official in charge who receives an application for registration of a change to a performance inspection agent under paragraph (3) shall verify the information for the applicable category below through the joint use of administrative information pursuant to Article 36(1) of the Electronic Government Act. However, where the applicant does not consent to verification by the public official in charge, the official shall require the relevant documents to be attached. <Amended 2017.3.9>
1. Where the trade name or the location of the principal place of business or a branch has changed: A copy of the business registration certificate or a certified copy of the corporate register (to be submitted only in the case of a corporation);
2. Where the corporation's representative or executive officers have changed: A certified copy of the corporate register;
3. Where the technical personnel employed have changed: Copies of the national technical qualification certificates of the new technical personnel.
⑤ The performance inspection agent registration certificate issued by the Mayor/Do Governor to a performance inspection agent pursuant to Article 14(3) of the Enforcement Decree shall be in attached Form 14. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26, 2020.9.8>

Article 15 (Standards for Administrative Dispositions against Performance Inspection Agents)
① The standards for revocation of registration or suspension of duties of a performance inspection agent under Article 29 of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 4.
② The Mayor/Do Governor may reduce or increase the period of suspension of duties specified in attached Table 4 by up to one-half of that period, taking into consideration the motives for the violation, the number of violations, and other relevant matters. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26, 2020.9.8>

Article 16 (Practical Education and Training Courses, etc.)
① The practical education conducted by the Minister of the Interior and Safety pursuant to Article 30(1) of the Act shall cover the knowledge and qualities required of a professional engineer engaged in an instrumentation business or in duties as a performance inspection agent, and the enhancement of understanding of relevant statutes, regulations, systems, and related matters. The education period shall not exceed 4 weeks. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
② Other details, including the subjects and methods of education and training and the criteria for recognition of completion, shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of the Interior and Safety. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>

Article 17 (Designation of Education Agencies, etc.)
① A specialized institution or organization concerned with disaster prevention (hereinafter referred to as a "specialized disaster prevention institution") intending to be designated as an agency for practical education pursuant to Article 30(2) of the Act shall satisfy the following requirements and submit an application for designation as an education agency in attached Form 15 (including an application in electronic form) to the Minister of the Interior and Safety. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. Classrooms with an area of at least 100 m² (excluding educational institutions specializing exclusively in online education);
2. At least 1 full-time instructor. However, where the number of persons educated annually is 10,000 or more, 1 additional full-time instructor shall be provided for every 10,000 such persons;
3. At least 1 staff member dedicated to the work.
② The Minister of the Interior and Safety shall issue a certificate of designation as an education agency in attached Form 16 to a specialized disaster prevention institution designated as an education agency pursuant to Article 30(2) of the Act and shall publicly notify the details of the designation. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
③ The Minister of the Interior and Safety or the head of an education agency designated under paragraph (2) shall issue a certificate of completion of education in attached Form 17 to a person who has completed an education and training course under Article 30(1) of the Act and Article 16 of this Rule. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
④ A person designated as an education agency under paragraphs (1) and (2) shall, when intending to conduct education and training for professional engineers engaged in an instrumentation business or in duties as a performance inspection agent, formulate an education and training plan for each training course and submit it to the Minister of the Interior and Safety. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>

